content:
Looking at the evidence, the worker rollback at t=590 (E15) has clearly taken effect — worker restarts stopped (E11, E12 show last restart at t=590, now 0.00/s), and throughput metrics recovered (E5, E7, E8, E9). However, 174 orphaned orders remain (E1, E10 shows queue_depth still at 406). These are orders that were created during the outage window (t=513–t=590) when the worker was crashing and not processing messages.

Before proposing the repair, I want to confirm the orphaned orders are genuinely unprocessed (not in a terminal state) and that there are no duplicate messages that could cause double-processing.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT m.state, COUNT(*) FROM messages m JOIN orders o ON m.order_id = o.id WHERE o.created_at >= 513 AND o.created_at <= 590 GROUP BY m.state",
      "why": "Confirm the orphaned orders have messages stuck in a non-terminal state, validating that requeue_orphaned_orders is the right repair."
    },
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT COUNT(*) as total_orphans, MIN(o.created_at) as first_created, MAX(o.created_at) as last_created FROM orders o WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM messages m WHERE m.order_id = o.id AND m.state IN ('pending','processing','done'))",
      "why": "Quantify orders with no live message to confirm the 174-violation count and the time window, ensuring requeue covers all affected orders."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "worker",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "Worker v1.0.1 deployed at t=485 caused repeated health-check failures and restarts from t=513, leaving queue messages unprocessed and accumulating 174 orphaned orders; rollback to v1.0 at t=590 stopped the crashes but did not re-enqueue the stranded messages.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E10", "E11", "E12", "E14", "E15"],
      "refuting": [],
      "explains": ["I2_no_orphaned_orders"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {"action": "requeue_orphaned_orders", "params": {}}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Worker v1.0.1 (deployed t=485) crashed repeatedly until rollback at t=590, leaving 174 orders with no live queue message; requeue_orphaned_orders will re-enqueue them for processing."
}
```
